      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_4e598185904513fccfe88348eaf17236aeead7f2789386182505548173083021",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The comparison separates two roles that the source assigns to the new representation: the hyperbolic denominator is meant to encode nonzero residue contributions, while the 1/y term removes the contribution at the origin. This gives a structural bridge from an integral kernel to alternating discrete data, unlike the neighboring Fermi–Dirac/Gamma and Ramanujan forms, but it neither establishes uniqueness or superiority nor supplies enough reliable detail here to fix the pole locations, residues, or contour.",
