    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_120105fdb2a9c2b3d70f697d34776d46b0310da442129f3ab0dbc02f8ef7448a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The exact kernel 1/y-1/sinh(y) combines two structural roles: its terms cancel the singular contribution at the origin, while the source attributes the remaining nonzero pole structure to the hyperbolic denominator and associates those residues with alternating discrete data. Read with the stated strip for the integral, the local subtraction accounts for the regularization needed near y=0 while preserving the residue-based connection to the alternating zeta representation.",
