    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_572199806c92e21433a4345f8751e0970745f4f44c88be494c82a0e71a29a7d8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The residue construction first engineers an integral whose residues reproduce the required n-power while leaving an alternating rational n-family that can be summed into the hyperbolic-kernel representation. The later section then rewrites that same kernel through sinh(y)-y, expands it into odd monomials, and evaluates the resulting Mellin-type terms to obtain Gamma(2n-s+1)zeta(2n-s+1); separately summing the Gamma-only series produces the displayed correction with zeta(2n-s+1)-1.",
